  "summary_en": "Eurofound report using survey data and case studies on how advanced, AI-enabled robots change work organisation and working conditions in EU workplaces. It argues for human-centric design, worker involvement, attention to psychosocial risks, and training, in the context of the Machinery Regulation and OSH rules.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Robots are not causing widespread job losses; job profiles change more than job numbers.",
   "Establishments focus on physical safety and overlook psychosocial risks of human–robot interaction.",
   "Negative outcomes stem from organisational and management choices rather than the technology itself.",
   "Policy should promote human-centric design, incentives, and ethical design guidelines.",
   "Social partners and training on digital skills and OSH implementation are essential."
